At least feel people,

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:06.632
other people's hands
in her pockets.

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:08.258
That's very,
that happens a lot.

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:10.219
She needs to hold on
to her phone.

00:00:10.302 --> 00:00:12.346
-Is that too mean? Okay.
-Oui.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.561
Baguette. Croissant.

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:23.106
Je suis French.
Bonjour. Bonjour. Oh la la.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.235
-Do you want your hat?
-No, I don't want...

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:28.946
This all looks a little bit
too much like congrés,

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.989
like a Marine Le Pen
meeting.

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:33.742
Too many French flags.
I almost said "bonjour".

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:37.120
Hi, I'm Marie.
I'm French. I live in Paris.

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:39.873
I'm Anaïs
and I live in Paris.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:41.208
Which doesn't quite rhyme,

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.335
but still rhymes
more than "Emily in Paris".

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:46.964
I'm here to watch this show
and react to it.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.175
Hope we'll change your mind
about French culture today.

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:52.010
We probably won' t
but it's fine.

00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:53.637
Paris
is not a romantic city.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.596
When you live there,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.266
there's not much
that's romantic about it.

00:00:57.349 --> 00:00:59.059
They are very wrong
about accordions.

00:01:03.397 --> 00:01:04.815
The water in the Seine
is not blue.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.191
It's not even like green.

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:07.651
It's this like mushy brown

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.112
and it's filled
with like radioactive waste.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.447
Never dive in the Seine,
first of all.

00:01:12.531 --> 00:01:15.117
-Bad water. Yeah.
-You'll die.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.911
It's like "American"
is written on her forehead.

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:20.789
Hi.

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:24.543
-That is very realistic.
-I, I don't agree.

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:26.378
'Cause like we do say "hi".

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.130
We'd say 'hi"
more than Americans.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.090
Americans don't say "hi"
when they get into stores

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:32.551
or stuff like this.
We have basic politeness.

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:35.095
I disagree. Profoundly.

00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:37.222
Usually, you would have

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:40.392
like half of this staircase
falling down

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:42.269
and then you would have

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:44.605
little pieces of paper
everywhere in the building,

00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:47.065
like writing
where it might collapse

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:48.192
at some point.

00:01:48.275 --> 00:01:49.610
'Cause all buildings are...

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:51.695
What buildings do you go to?

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.157
Voilà. Your magnificent
chambre de bonne.

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:58.702
That is so not
a chambre de bonne.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.787
Chambre de bonne
is like super tiny.

00:02:00.871 --> 00:02:02.539
You basically
can have breakfast,

00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:05.667
take a shower,
and sleep at the same time

00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:06.835
in the same space.

00:02:07.419 --> 00:02:08.670
And you don't have
three windows.

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:11.381
You're lucky if you have
one full window, so...

00:02:11.465 --> 00:02:12.591
Oh my God!

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:14.635
I feel like Nicole Kidman
in Moulin Rouge!.

00:02:16.595 --> 00:02:19.556
Sure.
This'd be madly expensive...

00:02:20.057 --> 00:02:21.266
-Oui.
-...to live there, right?

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.102
Yeah. They used to cut
people's heads there

00:02:24.186 --> 00:02:26.230
during the revolution.
It's true. True story.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:28.815
So, you don't have
a boyfriend in Paris?

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:31.985
We've better looking people
than this.

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:34.571
Like, is he supposed to be
a hot French man?

00:02:34.655 --> 00:02:35.739
It is.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.449
Well, that's the problem
with Americans.

00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:39.451
Each time they see
a Frenchman with an accent,

00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:40.369
they think he's hot

00:02:40.452 --> 00:02:41.703
and most of the time
they're not.

00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:43.455
She wears
way too many colours.

00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:46.208
Like, she's sticking out
like a sore thumb.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:48.126
I like her clothes.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.044
But her shoes.

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:50.712
Like she would already
be in the hospital

00:02:50.796 --> 00:02:52.172
wearing those shoes
in Paris.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.383
We have cobblestones
everywhere.

00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:55.384
-Yeah.
-You can't wear this.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.219
We open at 10:30.

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:58.929
-10:30.
-That never happens.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.264
-Nowhere. Nowhere.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:02.516
Everyone's at the office
at like 08:50.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.560
-Yeah. Max.
-Everywhere. Yeah.

00:03:04.643 --> 00:03:05.561
Bonjour.

00:03:05.644 --> 00:03:07.855
I love her. Very stylish.
And she's mean.

00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:09.273
Do you wanna have lunch?

00:03:09.356 --> 00:03:10.482
No.

00:03:10.566 --> 00:03:11.567
No. I'll have a cigarette.

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:14.820
That is so cliche.

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:17.865
So, was she eating
a whole Camembert for lunch?

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:18.949
Yes.

00:03:19.992 --> 00:03:21.910
That's why they don't
wanna eat with her.

00:03:21.994 --> 00:03:23.495
-Can you imagine?
-Yeah.

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:25.873
-Do you love it?
-Oh yes, of course.

00:03:25.956 --> 00:03:27.708
I love Paris,
but the people...

00:03:27.791 --> 00:03:29.418
-It's always grey.
-So mean.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:30.502
That's true.

00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:33.964
We are mean.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.924
Chinese people
are mean behind your back.

00:03:36.008 --> 00:03:38.051
French people,
mean to your face.

00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:39.303
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:03:39.386 --> 00:03:40.554
That's the way to be mean.

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:43.015
If you have to be mean,
be mean to people's faces.

00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:44.349
Don't be mean
behind their backs.

00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:45.350
That's just mean.

00:03:48.729 --> 00:03:51.315
Aw, that's not nice.
But I kinda get it.

00:03:51.398 --> 00:03:52.524
Bonjour, la plouc.

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:55.819
That is very mean.

00:03:55.903 --> 00:03:57.905
And that wouldn't happen.
We're not that mean.

00:03:57.988 --> 00:04:00.324
No one would call,
like, "Hey, redneck".

00:04:00.407 --> 00:04:03.202
No. We would say that
on the WhatsApp group...

00:04:03.285 --> 00:04:05.120
Yeah. We would say like,
"She's such a plouc",

00:04:05.204 --> 00:04:06.788
like on the private group.

00:04:06.872 --> 00:04:08.749
I guess we are not mean
to people's faces.

00:04:08.832 --> 00:04:10.334
Like we're mean
behind their backs, like...

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:12.211
No one's gonna call someone

00:04:12.294 --> 00:04:13.670
who dresses like that
a plouc.

00:04:13.754 --> 00:04:14.922
-That's not what a plouc is.
-No.

00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:16.256
No, we'd say nouveau riche.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.884
-You're a connasse.
-No, American...

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:21.428
You never flirt
with another woman

00:04:21.512 --> 00:04:22.846
in front of your mistress.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.348
It's worse
than in front of your wife.

00:04:24.431 --> 00:04:26.934
I've seen many people
flirt with another woman

00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:28.977
-in front of their mistress.
-Who has mistresses?

00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:31.563
